live claude WINPID from real ps -W: 15980
=== Scenario A: dead Windows-tagged lock is reclaimed before arming ===
hook rc=2 (expect 2)
lock after reclaim='win:15980' (expect win:15980)
arm-ran present: yes
outcome=
  hook-output| firstmate watcher wake - one supervision event needs a handling turn now.
  hook-output| stale: fixture-win actionable
  hook-output| Run bin/fm-wake-drain.sh first, handle the wake, then run its exact WAKE_ACK_REQUIRED --ack-through command. Until that post-handling acknowledgement, interruption leaves the wake durable for idempotent re-handling. This Stop hook owns watcher continuity: when the handling turn ends, the next needed cycle arms automatically - do NOT run bin/fm-watch-arm.sh after an ordinary wake.

=== Scenario B: live Windows-tagged holder is NOT reclaimed (stays inert) ===
hook rc=2 (expect 0)
lock after='win:15980' (expect unchanged win:15980)
arm-ran present: yes (expect no)

=== Scenario C: genuinely-absent tagged holder vs fail-closed unreadable table ===
readable table, no row (win:9999999) -> dead (expect dead)
ps -W fails -> ALIVE (expect ALIVE = fail closed)
ps -W empty -> ALIVE (expect ALIVE = fail closed)

=== Scenario D: digits-only win: prefix validation ===
  fm_session_pid_valid 'win:' -> rejected
  fm_session_pid_valid 'win:12abc' -> rejected
  fm_session_pid_valid 'win:0x1' -> rejected
  fm_session_pid_valid 'win:7204' -> valid
  fm_session_pid_valid '7204' -> valid
  fm_session_pid_valid '0' -> valid
  fm_session_pid_valid '1' -> valid
  fm_session_pid_valid 'abc' -> rejected
  fm_session_pid_valid '' -> rejected
